/*! \mainpage preC-SUMO Developer Guide

\tableofcontents

\section intro Introduction
preC-SUMO is the coupling-side adapter between D-FlowFM and C-SUMO in a preCICE setup.

Current core responsibilities are:
- read and validate C-SUMO settings,
- register preCICE meshes and data channels,
- receive far-field data from preCICE and write FF2NF input files,
- wait for and read NF2FF output files,
- convert NF2FF results to connected source/sink writes for D-FlowFM via preCICE.

For the underlying preCICE concepts and API details, see the external documentation:
- <a href="https://precice.org/docs.html">preCICE documentation</a>

For the canonical build and example workflow, see \ref build_and_run_example_12.

\section reading_path Recommended Reading Path
For a developer-oriented overview without opening the implementation, read the documentation in this order:
1. this page for the system overview and runtime workflow,
2. \ref build_and_run_example_12 for the concrete example setup and launch scripts,
3. the code entry points below when you want to map the design to implementation files.

\section coupling_workflow Core Coupling
The coupling between D-Flow FM and C-SUMO is handled using preCICE. The D-FlowFM has an adapter implementation which does the conversion between FM mesh/data to and from preCICE. 
The preC-SUMO executable is a wrapper that interacts with preCICE, writes FF2NF files that are consumed by the C-SUMO application, and reads the resulting NF2FF files, which are then sent to FM using preCICE.

\dotfile coupled_solvers_fm_csumo.dot "FM and preC-SUMO coupling overview"

\section architecture Architecture Overview
The system-level picture below shows the surrounding coupled components: D-Flow FM, the preCICE adapter,
C-SUMO, and the NF2FF/FF2NF exchange files.
\image html FM-C-SUMO_scheme_precice.drawio.svg "Coupled FM/C-SUMO architecture via preCICE" width=1000px
preCICE offers tools like config-visualizer which can be used to view the in use precice-config file.

